Paolo,

identifying patterns of any kind is tricky with small sample sizes. That is general to any kind of statistics, not specific to phylogenetic signal. Whether you want to go on and interpret this kind of patterns, when p<0.05, is a matter of personal decision of the researcher, I think. That is, it depends on how you interpret a p-value and how strict you want to be with your data...

Antigoni

