Dear Antigoni,

Thanks for your kind response

Of course! This is a more general question that is not only related to the specific test I mentioned. However, according to my knowledge a very small sample size affected the computation of the univariate Kappa statistic of Blomberg et al (2003), but according to simulations and the example presented in the generalization of the K statistics in Adams (2014) the Kmulti is a much more robust statistics. In the example of Adams (2014) he used also a small sample size (n <10) but he obtained significant p values. Obviously, this is a much more complex question that is beyond the Kmulti statistics but given the results of Adams (2014) I´m interested to know if in my specific case the small sample size can be an explanation for the lack of statistical significance.

Thanks,

Paolo

